title: 'Anthropic, "How we built our multi-agent research system" (2025): a brief needs an objective, an output, its tools and its boundaries; effort must be scaled to the task.'
pid: ff0f1806-c51b-4060-8878-a3065d6d64f1
body: |2-
  https://www.anthropic.com/engineering/multi-agent-research-system
  Multi-agent work used about 15 times the tokens of a chat, and fits
  poorly where agents must share context or depend on each other, as
  in coding. Vague briefs made subagents duplicate work. The lead
  saves its plan to memory so it survives the context being cut.
  Early versions spawned fifty subagents for simple questions, so
  they wrote explicit effort rules into the prompts. Outputs written
  to files and passed by reference avoid a game of telephone. One
  judging call with a rubric was the most consistent evaluator.
